      ],
      "riders": [
        "If you target the attacker and hit, apply one Form talent you know (the GM applies it, as Counter Palm does).",
        "If you target the weapon and hit, the weapon takes the attack's damage and may break if nonmagical and the damage meets its Damage Threshold; a magical/artifact/soul-bound weapon may resist with a Cultivation Check. No object-durability/breaking mechanic is modeled on this table -- GM adjudicates the weapon-targeting branch entirely.",
        "Ambiguity flagged for an owner ruling: the printed text never states an explicit Action Type (unlike Iron Forearm Guard and Counter Palm, which both say 'Action Type: Reaction'). It can only sensibly run off another creature's turn, so this entry infers Reaction econ and an Expend-Martial-Focus cost from context, matching its sibling Guard/Meridian reactions."
      ]
